{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1781549185955,"sessionID":"ses_1337021d0ffeym7DiJBLFLUi3w","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_HxDtOVHJZpPtxOihZFveN3av","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/incident_staffing_plan/answer/staffing_assignment.md","offset":1,"limit":300},"output":"<path>/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/incident_staffing_plan/answer/staffing_assignment.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ## Checkpoint 3: Final Assignment\n2: \n3: - Incident ID: `INC-4472`\n4: - Assignment window: `2026-05-06 18:00 to 2026-05-06 22:00`\n5: - Primary responder: `Ben`\n6: - Backup responder: `Deepa`\n7: \n8: ### Primary Choice\n9: \n10: `Ben` is the only responder who satisfies all primary rules: role `Database Engineer`, scheduled for `database` on-call coverage for the full window, available for the full window, active `db-prod` access after applying the 2026-05-04 access update, and fewer than 2 active incidents.\n11: \n12: ### Backup Choice\n13: \n14: `Deepa` is eligible for backup because she is an `SRE`, available for the full incident window, has active `db-prod` access, and has 0 active incidents. Among eligible backup candidates before final assignment, `Deepa` beats `Ben` on the fewest-active-incidents tie-breaker (0 vs 1), and using `Deepa` also preserves different people for primary and backup.\n15: \n16: ### Rejected Candidate Summary\n17: \n18: - `Asha` was rejected because she already has 2 active incidents.\n19: - `Carmen` was rejected because the newest access update suspended `db-prod` access.\n20: - `Eli` was rejected because the role is `Incident Manager`, not an eligible technical responder role.\n21: - `Farah` was rejected because she is not available for the full 18:00 to 22:00 window.\n22: - `Gabe` was rejected because the newest access update says `db-prod` access is still not provisioned, and he is not on `database` on-call for primary coverage.\n\n(End of file - total 22 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"## Checkpoint 3: Final Assignment\n\n- Incident ID: `INC-4472`\n- Assignment window: `2026-05-06 18:00 to 2026-05-06 22:00`\n- Primary responder: `Ben`\n- Backup responder: `Deepa`\n\n### Primary Choice\n\n`Ben` is the only responder who satisfies all primary rules: role `Database Engineer`, scheduled for `database` on-call coverage for the full window, available for the full window, active `db-prod` access after applying the 2026-05-04 access update, and fewer than 2 active incidents.\n\n### Backup Choice\n\n`Deepa` is eligible for backup because she is an `SRE`, available for the full incident window, has active `db-prod` access, and has 0 active incidents. Among eligible backup candidates before final assignment, `Deepa` beats `Ben` on the fewest-active-incidents tie-breaker (0 vs 1), and using `Deepa` also preserves different people for primary and backup.\n\n### Rejected Candidate Summary\n\n- `Asha` was rejected because she already has 2 active incidents.\n- `Carmen` was rejected because the newest access update suspended `db-prod` access.\n- `Eli` was rejected because the role is `Incident Manager`, not an eligible technical responder role.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/incident_staffing_plan/answer/staffing_assignment.md","text":"## Checkpoint 3: Final Assignment\n\n- Incident ID: `INC-4472`\n- Assignment window: `2026-05-06 18:00 to 2026-05-06 22:00`\n- Primary responder: `Ben`\n- Backup responder: `Deepa`\n\n### Primary Choice\n\n`Ben` is the only responder who satisfies all primary rules: role `Database Engineer`, scheduled for `database` on-call coverage for the full window, available for the full window, active `db-prod` access after applying the 2026-05-04 access update, and fewer than 2 active incidents.\n\n### Backup Choice\n\n`Deepa` is eligible for backup because she is an `SRE`, available for the full incident window, has active `db-prod` access, and has 0 active incidents. Among eligible backup candidates before final assignment, `Deepa` beats `Ben` on the fewest-active-incidents tie-breaker (0 vs 1), and using `Deepa` also preserves different people for primary and backup.\n\n### Rejected Candidate Summary\n\n- `Asha` was rejected because she already has 2 active incidents.\n- `Carmen` was rejected because the newest access update suspended `db-prod` access.\n- `Eli` was rejected because the role is `Incident Manager`, not an eligible technical responder role.\n- `Farah` was rejected because she is not available for the full 18:00 to 22:00 window.\n- `Gabe` was rejected because the newest access update says `db-prod` access is still not provisioned, and he is not on `database` on-call for primary coverage.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":22,"totalLines":22,"truncated":false}},"title":"tasks/incident_staffing_plan/answer/staffing_assignment.md","time":{"start":1781549185931,"end":1781549185950}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_097ed3aec73eed7b016a304881db6481919fa1023a6499dadb"}},"id":"prt_ecc9b3b87001XrU5v2JxZ28Fqo","sessionID":"ses_1337021d0ffeym7DiJBLFLUi3w","messageID":"msg_ecc9b29f5001rtw0t5m2m2MXYL"}}
